Telephony requests from registered agents

Remission applications from registered agents must be submitted through OSfA.

Where access to OSfA is not possible, applications may be taken by phone but must be referred to the dedicated remissions team, regardless of the remission amount.

Information

FC staff may continue to accept telephony requests from registered agents when directing them online would have a detrimental outcome.

Registered agents may continue to use inbound telephony to:

enquire about the progress of a remission request
submit further information as requested by the dedicated remissions team
seek clarification on or review of a previous refusal decision.

If a registered agent requests remission over the phone, advise them that all remission requests must be lodged through OSfA with the correct form attached. Refer to: 

