ATO fuel response payment plan requests

D-1 - This page explains to FS staff how to action requests regarding ATO fuel response payment plan.

Last published 1 July 2026

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

D-1

This page contains information on how to assist taxpayers applying for the ATO fuel response payment plan.

On 30 March 2026, the Australian Government announced the National Fuel Security Plan in response to pressures on Australia’s fuel supplies and prices. Taxpayers that met criteria for a Fuel Response Payment Plan could submit a request between 1 April 2026 to 30 June 2026.

Fuel response payment plan requests in Siebel IIA

A note will be present in the Siebel Internal Initiated Action (IIA) tab titled ATO Fuel Response Payment Plan Approved.

To identify if the request submission was sent by the taxpayer or tax agent, review the Reference Field which will display as either Fuel Response - Client initiated or Fuel Response - Tax agent initiated. This was not available for earlier IIA notes.

Apology communication issued

Some taxpayers may have received 2 different payment plan confirmation letters in error or were entered into a Fuel Response payment plan when their EOI only requested a PAYGI variation.

Apology emails were issued to affected taxpayers advising which letter to disregard and a note will be present in the Siebel Internal Initiated Action (IIA) tab titled ATO fuel response apology.

If you are actioning an inbound call regarding this:

confirm the taxpayer is affected by locating the IIA note

and for

2 letters apology: if appropriate, advise the correct letter is titled Confirming your Fuel Response payment plan and support the taxpayer using the email template on the IIA note and active payment plan details in ICP

PAYGI variation apology: if they want a Fuel Response payment plan or their original payment plan reinstated, take the appropriate actions in this procedure.

