Why some debts on hold are not in the account balance

The ATO implemented a new system in November 2023. From this date, debts on hold remain in the account balance. Before this when a debt was placed on hold, it was removed from the account balance so the pause on recovery actions could take effect. This made it confusing for some taxpayers who may have believed their debt no longer existed. Always listen to the taxpayer and be empathetic to the situation.

Some taxpayers may be frustrated or confused, and conversations may be difficult to navigate. If the discussion escalates, refer to Handling angry/abusive taxpayers & unprofessional agents.
