In Detail
Overview of ECA

In February 2024, the ATO re-commenced the use of ECA. ECA only collect debt on the specific cases referred to them. They commenced actioning these referrals as of 5 February 2024.

ECA negotiate with taxpayers for payment in full, or where appropriate, enter into a payment plan. If a new debt arises on a case, they will also start collection on this debt if the original debt is unpaid.

They:

adhere to strict privacy and professionalism guidelines
report to us monthly on their progress and adherence to these guidelines.

Collection agencies and their staff meet all Commonwealth secrecy and privacy requirements.

ECA currently have limited access to ATO systems. This allows them to:

provide real time and accurate information to taxpayers
action simple ATO taxpayer queries such as updating
addresses
taxpayer contact information (including authorised contacts).
