Procedure for Frontline Services Support to action External Collection Agency (ECA) enquiries.

Last published 22 January 2026

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

This procedure is for Frontline Services Support (FSS) to action External Collection Agency (ECA) enquiries.

ECA may call to request ATO technical advice or supporting actions to be completed on a taxpayer's account.

Recent updates

22/01/2026

	Update to 'Interest and penalty remission'.	SD-100692


01/12/2025

	Update to 'Payment methods'.	SD-99533
Checks
Confirm PORO and taxpayer details

Before discussing the account:

confirm ECA details
Opens in a new window
 are listed against the case. The ECA operator will advise they are from 'Recoveries Corporation Offsite'
confirm and take note of the following details with the ECA operator
their full name
user ID
that PORO has been successfully completed (items of proof do not need to be confirmed)
relevant taxpayer identifier
full name
TFN or ABN
you will also provide your name/user ID to the ECA operative at the end of your call to be recorded within their system notes.
Authorisations

ECAs have specified authorisations and delegations.
Opens in a new window
 Ensure all enquiries are governed by these authorisations.

Procedure Steps

If you have provided a decision, or taken any action on the taxpayers account, create an inbound call activity and note as per the relevant steps in this procedure. This could include, but is not limited to:

payment plan refusal or approval

remission approval/refusal

withdrawal decision

hardship or release consideration/escalation.

If you identify that it is necessary, peer to peer feedback
Opens in a new window
 can be provided for the ECA debt officer to ensure constructive advice has been provided. E.g. You have identified a skill development opportunity, incorrect advice has been provided to a taxpayer, or incorrect actions have been taken.

Create Siebel activity

For scenarios:

Actioning a remission request, or
Direct Debit bank account arrangement approval.

The ECA operator has already created an activity, you need to assign this activity to yourself and continue to complete all actions as per the procedures below.

For all other scenarios, go to the taxpayer's Consolidated Client View (CCV) in Siebel. Create an inbound call activity with the following classifications:

Capability: Debt case
Category: Collection negotiation
Type: ECA Referral
Interaction: Inbound phone
PORO: Not required
Status: In Progress.

Where instructed to follow an additional procedure, ensure to create a secondary activity
Opens in a new window
 as per relevant procedures to record actions taken.

Go to the relevant reasons for assistance below.

Updating taxpayer details
Payment plan
Payment methods
Missing payment search
MASCOT search
Interest and penalty remission
Hardship or release request
Credit or payment transfer
Technical advice to ECA
Guidance on incarcerated or overseas taxpayers
Guidance on complaints
Escalation required.
