debt amount
payment amount
payment frequency
payment method
taxpayer circumstances to justify the reason for a longer-term arrangement
capacity to pay (CTP) information that has been obtained from the taxpayer.

Determine if the ECA operative has obtained the relevant information regarding the taxpayers circumstances or gathered CTP.  If:

yes, all required information has been obtained go to step 2
no,
advise the ECA that they will need to go back to the taxpayer to obtain the details before a decision can be made
this is the end or the procedure.



2

	

Based on the information gathered at step 1, assess the taxpayer circumstances and make a decision or recommendation. 

If you are:

refusing and it is within your delegation, go to step 3
approving and it is within your delegation, go to step 4
recommending approval as it is outside of your delegation, go to step 5.



3

	

If your decision is to refuse the payment plan proposal from the ECA:

inform the ECA of your decision and educate them on the reasons why you are refusing
ask them to continue negotiating a more suitable arrangement with the taxpayer or advise of the next best actions.

