request the ECA Siebel activity ID
add a note
Opens in a new window
 advising of the reason for refusal and any actions to be taken by the ECA
do not update the activity status. This will be actioned by the ECA
action a refusal letter where appropriate.

If the request was for any other payment method:

update the inbound call activity
Notes: add a note
Opens in a new window
 using the ECA referral template in the Notes fly-out tab
Finalisation Code: Payment Plan Refusal
Status: Done
this is the end of the procedure.



4

	

Note: If the approval is outside your delegation, go to step 5.

If your decision is to approve the payment plan proposal from the ECA and it is within your authorisation, check the arrangement method. If:

via Direct Debit
request the ECA Siebel activity ID
activate the arrangement in ICP
update the ECA activity
Notes: add a note
Opens in a new window
 using the ECA referral template in the Notes fly-out tab
Finalisation Code: Arrangement granted
Status: Done
via any other payment method
advise the ECA debt officer of your approval and to input the arrangement into their system (do not enter the arrangement into ATO systems)
to record a note in their system regarding the approval and payment arrangement
provide them with your User ID and name for the approval record
update the inbound call activity
Notes: add a note
Opens in a new window
 using the ECA referral template in the Notes fly-out tab
Finalisation Code: Payment Plan – Approved
Status: Done.

This is the end of the procedure.




5

	

If you are supporting the decision to escalate for approval that is outside of your authorisation:

inform the ECA
that the decision is outside of your authorisation
Opens in a new window
, and
you need to escalate it for approval and they will be provided a decision within 48 hours
add a note
Opens in a new window
 to your inbound call activity using the ECA referral template in the Notes fly-out tab
escalate the request as per APS 6 approval required.
