Procedure to establish correspondence PORO.

Last published 21 May 2026

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

This provides the procedure to establish PORO for inbound correspondence.

Correspondence includes:

white mail (written correspondence), and
forms and unstructured messages received through Online services such as
Online services for business, or
Online services for agents.

Email should only be used for general enquiries.

PORO must be completed on:

white mail attached to a form, or

a note written on the form.

PORO is not required for white mail or emails received from courts in relation to matters before the court where the ATO is a party.

Warning

Taxpayer details must not be disclosed during interactions with court officials. Only general information can be provided by the ATO.

Information pre-printed on the form cannot be used to complete PORO. Anything written by the taxpayer can be used to complete PORO. Any instructions on the activity statement must pass white mail PORO.

Information alert:
Review all linked attachments and service request activities to assess the appropriate PORO requirements for the correspondence type. Ensure that no authorisations are missed.

