To ensure Siebel notes are consistent and contain quality information, do not use general or user customised VIPER note templates.

Record a document received

Where you receive a document directly from a taxpayer, before sending for back scanning, add a note including the following:

type of document
date of the document
date the document was received
author of the document, and
a brief summary of the key points of the document.
Third party authorisation discussions

Include in your note:

name of the authorised contact (include name of organisation/ TAN where applicable)
roles the authorised contact can access
phone number of authorised contacts, and
length of time the contact is authorised to act on the taxpayer's behalf.
IAL and Debt Assist staff requirements

Your payment conversation will be recorded in your lodgment activity. Your note should record your decisions and any actions taken, including:

type of payment plan granted
payment plan conditions provided
pre-legal warning provided, or if the taxpayer advises no requirement to provide
reason for
granting or refusing payment plan
not discussing the debt with the taxpayer
if additional information is required, specify a set date for receipt of this information.
TFN application processing

All actions and decisions taken to progress a TFN application must be recorded in your note.

Some of the procedures to action suspense errors for TFN applications have a note template included. These templates can be relied upon for a quality note. However, if additional actions or decisions were taken to those specified in the template, these should also be included in the note.

It is beneficial for any suspense error numbers to be included in the note so the actions and decisions can be linked to the original issue.

