Determining entity size

In applying FTL penalty, the Commissioner must determine the size of the entity at the date a document is required to be lodged. The size can be determined using an entity's income, turnover or withholder status under subsection 286-80 (3), (4) or (4A)
Opens in a new window
 of Schedule 1 of the TAA. The base penalty amount is increased if the entity is a medium or large entity.

The Commissioner will not always have the current information available to determine the correct size of an entity in accordance with the size tests as prescribed in the law. Consequently, the Commissioner will generally use the entity's withholder status to determine an entity's size. Where an entity does not have a large or medium withholder status and there is no evidence on hand justifying a higher rate, then the base penalty is applied.

An entity's size can be determined by viewing the PAYG withholding (PAYGW) role type in ICP.
