How to view statement of account (SoA) options and generate SoA correspondence in ICP

Last published 26 November 2024

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

This procedure describes how to view statement of account (SoA) options and generate SoA correspondence in the Integrated Core Processing (ICP) system.

Statements of account are used to:

assist taxpayers to make a payment

convey information regarding a taxpayer's obligations and explanatory messages

provide taxpayers with an accurate description of account activity

enable taxpayers to reconcile their account, and/or

provide taxpayers with necessary information to complete a form such as assessable income and deductible interest expenses.

Recent updates
30/08/2023	Added new content to 'Checks' and 'Scenarios'.	SD-72572
Checks
Review transactions

Check that the transactions on the account look correct as you work your way through the procedure. The issuing of incorrect refunds is a significant risk and has the potential to undermine the integrity of the tax system.

To report any identified incorrect credits or refunds, refer to Reporting an incorrect credit/refund.
Opens in a new window

It is important that you follow the above to reduce the risk of incorrect credit/refunds.

Lodgment reminder pilot

Review the Internal Initiated Action tab in Siebel to check if the taxpayer is part of the Lodgment Reminder Pilot.

For more information, refer to:

STP and activity statements - ATO PAYGW pre-fill
Opens in a new window
Activity statements - Lodgment Reminder Strategy.
Opens in a new window
Scenarios
Lodgment reminder strategy - Impacts to SoA

For the 23/2024 financial year, we will pilot the Activity Statements - Lodgment Reminder Strategy
Opens in a new window
 with 3,000 randomly selected Small and Medium employers.

Lodgment reminder letter will be issued if an employer doesn't lodge their activity statement. We will provide a timeframe to lodge and correct their activity statements. 

If they do not lodge their activity statement by the due date in the letter, amounts we have on record that are due and payable are added to their Integrated Client Account. These amounts include:

PAYG withholding amounts reported through STP, and
if applicable

GST Instalment amount, and / or
PAYGI (amount method only).

Individual postings for each role type will be displayed in the SoA and will not have the 'roll-up' function and instead will be on single line items. Contra-postings for variations will also appear on individual postings and not in a rollup feature.

Sort the SoA via effective date when viewing the SoA. This will group role type postings by the AS effective date. 

Information alert:
Different AS roles will finalise at different times, depending on when the Commissioner was notified. The BAS will not be finalised until all roles have been finalised.

Procedure Steps
Before you begin

All screens in the View SoA functionality are available to view through ICP and the business and Tax Agent Portals. View SoA options will only include account information for those roles currently deployed to ICP.

The system default values on the specified View SoA screens are:

financial year - the current year, and

ordered by field - the processed date.

If less than 40 transactions are available for the current financial year, the start date of the transactions displayed will be backdated until:

40 transactions are displayed, or

no further transactions are available for display.

Note: All transactions for the date of the 40th transaction will be displayed.

The maximum number of transactions which can be displayed is 498.

The transactions for a specific role can be viewed on the View SoA screen.

There is a difference in the date format between descriptions of converted transactions and those processed in ICP. Converted transactions have a date format of DD MMM YY (for example 01 Jul 08), while transactions processed in ICP have a date format of DD/MM/YYYY (for example 01/07/2008).

The user has access to update the SoA parameters to change the view criteria and/or request the data to be sent to outbound to generate correspondence to the taxpayer.

Be aware that the following business rules apply to SoA:

a payment slip will not be generated if a cheque or EFT is to be issued on the same SoA

the SoA will always default to a cheque if an EFT and cheque disbursement is to be issued on the same SoA.

 The action required to cancel a SoA in ICP will depend on how it was generated.

Where the SoA was generated by a transaction being posted to the account a SoA request transaction will be generated. Where the status of the SoA request transaction is:

Pending or Approved, cancel the transaction following Request transaction - view and modify request
Opens in a new window

Processed, cancel the SoA in outbound (if prior to the issue date) following Search & maintain - cancel outbound correspondence
Opens in a new window

Where you have manually generated the SOA request in line with this procedure, no SOA request transaction will be generated. The SOA should be cancelled in outbound following Search & maintain - cancel outbound correspondence.
Opens in a new window

