D-1 - Options available for supporting taxpayers with valid reasons for being unable to pay an outstanding debt.

Last published 22 June 2026

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

D-1

This page provides guidance on support options available to taxpayers with valid reasons for being unable to pay an outstanding debt.

While we seek to understand a taxpayer’s circumstances and provide appropriate support, we cannot:

change tax outcomes
remove tax debts, or
alter legislated obligations.

We will clearly communicate what we can and cannot do within the law and our role as the tax administrator.

Where obligations have been genuinely incurred and remain payable, our role is to listen with empathy, and support taxpayers to meet their obligations in the best way available, including through:

appropriate payment options
tailored engagement, and
referrals to additional support where relevant.

Operation Protego activities impact taxpayer advice/treatment. Ensure you confirm the taxpayer is not identified for Operation Protego activities before proceeding.

Taxpayers impacted by Operation Protego Activities can be identified either via:

2022 Operation Protego Siebel Alert, or
having a credit suppression and Siebel note/activity description referencing #operationprotego.
