Procedure Steps
Step
	Action
1	

Go to IPS.


2	

Select Search (binocular icon).


3	

Type in the ABN or TFN and the relevant Integrated Client Account (ICA) role.

If the ICA is other than '001', over type with the appropriate ICA role number in the CAC field.


4	

Select Search.

A list of all activity statements will display.

Use the black double arrows on the right side to scroll to older periods.

If no documents are issued, this message will display: 'No activity statement found for the requested search criteria'. In this case, ensure you have selected the correct ICA role.




5

	

Check the status of the activity statement.

A status of:

DSP means the activity statement remains outstanding

RCVD means the document has been received but not fully processed

FIN means the document has been received and finalised

DISC means the activity statement has been terminated (discontinued)

CANC means the activity statement has been cancelled. 

If the status is 'DISC' or 'CAN', check notes and with the taxpayer to confirm no lodgment is required. 




6

	

Check the Milestone of the activity statement to obtain more information. Complete the following:

from the Activity Statement list window, highlight the form
select
