Procedure to action non-lodgment advice for correspondence and phone.

Last published 1 July 2026

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

This is a procedure for actioning a non-lodgment advice (NLA), including self-service options for individuals, agents and practitioners.

When a taxpayer has assessed themselves as not needing to lodge a tax return, they may:

provide non-lodgment advice for a particular tax return (recorded as a return is not necessary (RNN) in ICP), or
advise they have no obligation to lodge further returns (recorded as a Further return not necessary (FRNN) in ICP).

These notifications can be provided via the taxpayer's preferred channel to ensure they meet their tax obligations.

This QuickNav provides a tailored view of Action non-lodgment advice.
