The ATO has an RNN concession for newly registered SMSFs which have not commenced operating in their first year of registration. This concession allows super funds to be exempt from lodging an annual return and only applies to the first year. Written evidence is required to show:

the fund held assets in the second financial year, and
the date the assets were first held.

