D-1 - Information to assess remission requests for general interest charges (GIC).

Last published 19 September 2024

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

D-1

Information to assist with the decision-making process when actioning a remission request for general interest charges (GIC).

The purpose of GIC is to:

encourage the timely payment of tax
deny late payers an unfair financial advantage over those who pay on time, and
compensate the Australian Government and the community for the impact of late payments.

The desired outcome is to achieve a decision that is consistent with both the law and Practice Statement Law Administration PS LA 2011/12
Opens in a new window
 - Remission of General Interest Charge.

Clients will need to satisfy us that remission is warranted, considering the nature of the specific event.

The exercise of power to remit must also:

be fair to the whole community
address unfair financial advantage
uphold community expectations.
