Requests involving GST Property Credits

The credit on the supplier's GST property credits account is transferred into the supplier's activity statement account on the date the relevant activity statement is lodged.

The effective date of the GST property credit transfer posting is the date the activity statement is lodged. So, if the activity statement is lodged after the due date, the GIC becomes payable.

When considering a GIC remission request:

only consider the client's reason for not lodging the relevant activity statement on time
the fact the GST property credit was paid into the GST property credits account at the time of the sale is not grounds for a remission.

