In Detail
Financial difficulties

An individual or business can be considered to have financial difficulties when unexpected or extenuating circumstances leave them unable to pay their debt for a short period of time.

For more information, refer to Tax support for individuals, businesses, not-for-profits and tax professionals.
Opens in a new window
 

Serious hardship

Serious hardship can occur when an individual is experiencing vulnerability such as:

homelessness
family violence, or
financial coercion.

It can also occur when a primary tax debt will result in them being left without the means to pay for basic needs such as:

food

clothing

medical supplies

accommodation, and

education for themselves, their family or dependents.

For more information, refer to Tax support for individuals, businesses, not-for-profits and tax professionals.
