Background

This page is for trained staff in the Specialised Client Support (SCS) team only.

If you are not trained and:

taxpayer is experiencing financial difficulty or serious hardship warm transfer to Hardship Team x92176
taxpayer is experiencing immediate and severe vulnerability with threats of self-harm, domestic or family violence or coercion, warm transfer to Specialised Client Support Team x92196.

This page instructs trained FS Debt Assist staff how to process refund requests where the taxpayer reports:

hardship
exceptional circumstances
significant cash flow issues.

This procedure begins when:

you have been allocated an activity in Siebel via iWD or phone, and
it is a request from a taxpayer (or their representative) for their tax refund not to be offset against other taxation debts.

For a definition of serious hardship, refer to:

Tax support for individuals, businesses, not-for-profits and tax professionals,
