Procedure Steps
Task 1 - Reply to message

Complete steps below. Start in the Siebel Activity Details view of the inbound activity you are replying to.

Step	Action


1

	

To be able to respond via online services, they must have sent a message to the ATO via online services. This is determined by the Receipt ID beginning with 501.

Go to the Related Receipt ID field and ensure the receipt ID begins with 501. If:

yes, go to step 2
no,
initiate a secure message
Opens in a new window
 via online services, or
find an alternative method to respond to the taxpayer or agent
this is the end of the procedure.




2

	

Select Reply.

The Service Request Detail view is displayed.

An outbound correspondence activity is automatically created and linked via a Service Request (SR) to the original activity.




 3

	

Select the Activity ID hyperlink for the Outbound Correspondence activity just created.




4

	

Check if the Classification of the activity is correct. If:

yes, go to step 5
no, reclassify the activity.
Opens in a new window

The default classification of the outbound activity created when replying will be the same as the inbound activity.


5	

If you need to add this activity to a case:

type the case ID into the Case ID field
go to task 2.
Task 2 - Construct message

Complete steps below.

Step	Action


1

	

Select the Correspondence tab to confirm the destination channel. 

The channel selected should be the same as the channel the original activity generated from. If not, the message will not send. For secure messages to be sent to BAS agents or tax agents, select TAP.

Go to the Destination Channel field and select appropriate channel from the drop-down list. If you cannot see the destination channel, select Show more.

If the channel is:

Online services for agents,
select TAP
go to step 2
Online services for business,
select BP
go to step 3.



2

	

Go to the TAN field to check the agent's registered agent number (RAN) has been populated. If:

yes, go to step 3
no, 
populate the agent's RAN into the TAN field
go to step 3.

When replying via OSfA, the response will always go to the agent who originally sent the secure message. In most instances the TAN field will be pre-populated and must not be changed or the message will not send.




3

	

Go to the Unstructured Mail Message field. If the unstructured message field is not visible, expand the Siebel window with the arrows in the top right corner.




4

	

Type the required message:

Refer to Siebel - secure message guidelines and principles
Opens in a new window
 for examples and message protocols, including guidelines for 

gender neutral salutations 
signatures, and
attachments.

Before sending, check the message for:

incorrect taxpayer or agent name
spelling errors
punctuation errors
inaccurate information
content that does not make sense
formatting issues (spacing, alignment, font colours)
chevrons < > indicating variable text (these should be removed).



5

	

Save the record (use Ctrl + S or select Options Menu (COG wheel)).




6

	

Check if an attachment is required. If:

yes, go to task 3
no, go to task 4.
Task 3 - Add an attachment

If more than 6 attachments are required to an online services message create additional replies.

You must ensure the correct attachment is attached to the activity to restrict privacy breaches. All 'read only' attachments are to be sent in PDF format.

Follow the steps below to add an attachment to a secure message.

Step	Action


1

	

Ensure the attachment to be added has been checked by a peer for any errors and corrected where required. These include:

incorrect taxpayer or agent name
spelling errors
punctuation errors
inaccurate information
content that does not make sense
formatting issues (spacing, alignment, font colours)
chevrons < > indicating variable text (these should be removed).



2

	

Attach and publish all attachments required for the message. 

You must ensure the correct attachment is attached to the activity to prevent privacy breaches. 

Do not include your User ID in document names as this will be visible to the recipient.

All 'read only' attachments are to be sent in PDF format. There is a limit of 6 attachments per message at 6MB per attachment. 




3

	

Highlight the row containing the new attachment in the Attachments list.




4

	

Select Publish. Siebel will publish the selected attachment to the Inbound Outbound Data Library (IODL).

The Document ID field in the Attachments list will populate with the new unique Document ID. If this has not automatically populated within a few minutes, refresh the screen.




5

	

Save the record (use Ctrl + S or select Options Menu (COG wheel)).

Task 4 - Send the secure message

Complete steps below.

Step	Action


1

	

Select Send Correspondence in the Activity Details screen.

The Correspondence Sent Date is updated with the current date.

The update to the outbound activity may not happen immediately. The activity will update once the activity has been sent. 

You will need to refresh the activity for the Status field to be set to Done. Select:

Home tab
SR ID of the original inbound activity
hyperlink in the Activity ID field of the outbound correspondence activity that you created.

If the status has not been updated, do not select the Send Correspondence button again. This will generate a second message to the taxpayer or agent.




2

	

Select Menu, then Save Record.

Do not change the status field of the outbound activity to 'Done'. It will auto finalise.

Once the activity auto finalises, the correspondence will show up as an attachment in the activity.




3

	

Check if the message transmission was successful. If related receipt ID (RRI) starts with:

10, and receipt ID is 
different to RRI, then outcome is failed
same as RRI, then outcome is successful
50, and receipt ID starts with 10, then outcome is successful.
Information

You can also access the staff view of OSfA or OSB to confirm if the secure message is appearing in the relevant inbox:

go to ATOO for the agent or taxpayer
view the relevant inbox to confirm the secure message has been received.

If:

yes, go to task 5
no, and the issue

can be resolved, take corrective action then go to task 5
cannot be resolved,

add a note to advise transmission was unsuccessful
source an alternative way to send the message to the taxpayer or agent, and 
go to task 5.
Task 5 - Finalise activity

If you were directed to this procedure by another process, and there are further actions to complete, return to that process.

Otherwise finalise the Inbound Siebel activity as follows:

Status: Done
delete any saved documents from your share drive or desktop once you have successfully sent the correspondence.
