In Detail
Pre-call SMS

Where you have identified a need to attempt phone contact with taxpayers or registered agents (for example, to advise the outcome or evidence required) issue a Pre-call SMS.
Opens in a new window

This SMS advises the taxpayer or registered agent that they will receive a call from the ATO (in the time frame selected) and that it will come from a private number.

Information

If SMS is not possible (for example, the 1 to 1 tool is unavailable) continue to attempt phone contact.

Call Screening

Some taxpayers use the 'call screening' feature on their device to save time or block unwanted calls.

When the device detects a new or unknown number, it silently answers and prompts the caller to state their name and reason for calling.

The caller's response is converted to text and shown on the recipient's screen. The recipient then decides whether to answer or ignore the call.

Warning

You must not disclose any personal, protected, sensitive or account-related information during the call screening portion of the call.

If you receive a call screening message indicating the recipient is using a screening service:

identify yourself clearly by stating
you are calling from the ATO
your full name, and
your work area
provide a brief waiting message, such as: 'Please answer or return the call when available. I will wait one minute to allow you to answer the call'.

For example, you could say: 'I am an ATO officer calling. Please answer or return the call when available. I will wait one minute to allow you to answer the call'.

This will ensure the recipient:

receives a transcript that clearly identifies you, and
understands they have approximately one minute to respond before the call ends.

If the call screening service forwards you to voicemail, go to Leaving messages (if appropriate).

Dialler campaigns

If contact is not made on the first attempt:

try all available numbers until contact is made or a message is left, where there is facility to do so

if appropriate, issue a Post-call SMS
Opens in a new window

when a message is left or contact is unsuccessful, update the case as per Debt - Outbound contact attempted
Opens in a new window

when taxpayer contact could not be made, consider desktop tracing.
Opens in a new window
 For example

phone number is disconnected

contact is no longer associated with the taxpayer, or

there are no other phone numbers listed in Siebel and ICP

where desktop tracing has been taken, discuss with your team leader if case ownership is required.

Where subsequent contact attempts are required, review:

previous dialler campaign notes to help identify the most suitable number with which to commence contact

ICP for alternative numbers not previously attempted.

Hours of contact

The taxpayer's location determines the hours of contact. Check which state/territory you are calling, and note:

any time zone differences,
Opens in a new window
 or
public holidays in that state/territory before making outbound contact.

Check the appropriate hours of contact for the taxpayer type:

Registered agents: Monday to Friday, 9:00 am to 6:00 pm

All other taxpayers:

Monday to Friday, 8:00 am to 8:00 pm

Saturday, 9:00 am to 5:00 pm.

Cases are delivered based on the location of the taxpayer. If calling an agent, you will need to confirm it is after 9:00 am in their location.

Warning
alert:
Compare the taxpayer contact details with the registered agent details to ensure you are only attempting contact with a registered agent within the above hours of contact.
Call recording

When calling from an area where call recording is active, provide a warning to each person you speak with that:

this call is being recorded to improve our service

if they do not want this call to be recorded, advise so now.

Stop call recording
Opens in a new window
 if requested.

Warning
alert:
It is an offence to record a phone call without the knowledge of one or more parties to that call. You must advise all parties to each call that the call is being recorded. Failure to do so will put you in breach of Subsection 7(1) of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act (TIA Act).

Privacy notice

For all outbound calls, where a taxpayer record is being discussed, a privacy notice must be provided as soon as practicable to each authorised person you speak to.

